(29)
If the basis is obtained via the unmodified POD, it can be shown that, at the same time and parameter values of the snapshots, the orthogonal error of a kth order ROM is given by


‖e⊥priori(t,μ)‖F=∑j=k+1rλj2
(30)
It can then be deduced that when k = r the orthogonal error is null. The following equation


