and the previous equation (30) can be used to control the orthogonal error at the snapshot points before even doing ROM calculations, in other words, it is an a priori error measure. In Petzold and Rathinam,60 error bounds were derived for the case of the POD-Galerkin reduction of a nonlinear ODE. For the same parameters and inputs, the total and collinear error over time can be bounded by using the orthogonal error
||e//(t)|| L2<||e⊥(t)|| L2
(32)
||et(t)|| L2<γ' r||e⊥(t)|| L2
(33)
Here 
γ' r
