Two methods applicable to any type of ROM will be presented next.
The Leave-one-out cross validation, presented in Braconnier et al.,62 supposes that the parameter space or region to explore has been partitioned in r partitions, each with its own sample of the HDM. The leave-one-out cross validation error for a snapshot with parameter set μk is then given by
E(μk)=‖w(μk)-V-kq(μk)-k‖2
(34)
Here 
V-k
